{- Regression: a multi-arm case in a constructor-cell field must compile on
   the JVM. `IO.Stdout.print (case x of …)` puts the case into a field of the
   lowered `IOStdoutPrint` cell — the lazy-IO lowering routes every user
   expression handed to an IO platform built-in through a constructor field —
   and the JVM emitter used to reject the shape with an internal error
   ("unified emitter gate missed value"): a multi-arm case emits StackMapTable
   frames that declare an empty operand stack, which the half-built cell on
   the stack would contradict. The emitter now evaluates such fields into save
   locals first (`emitCellI`), the same discipline call arguments always had.
   The case below survives to codegen on purpose: a variable scrutinee with a
   multi-arm body is exactly the shape `Awsum.Simplify` leaves in place. -}

import IO.Stdout

f : Maybe Int32 -> IO Never Unit
f x = IO.Stdout.print (case x of
  Nothing -> "n"
  Just n -> showInt32 n)

main : IO Never Unit
main = f (Just (1 : Int32))
